CORE
main.c
-I broken --signed-overflow-check --no-assertions
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
^failed to preprocess or parse the CPROVER library models$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
The CPROVER library models are preprocessed together with the host's system
headers. When one is missing (on ciuccio, <asm/errno.h> under -m32 once
gcc-multilib was removed) preprocessing fails for the whole batch, abort()
loses its __CPROVER_assume(0) body, and the analysis went on to report an
overflow on a path abort() should have cut (weaver/loop-tiling-eq.wvr.c, a
false no-overflow alarm). broken/errno.h simulates the missing header on any
host. The library failure must stop the analysis, not change its verdict.
